+      <dl newline="true" spacing="normal" indent="3" pn="section-2-1">
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.1">IAC WILL X-DISPLAY-LOCATION</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.2">Sender is willing to send the X display location in a
+subsequent sub-negotiation.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.3">IAC WON'T X-DISPLAY-LOCATION</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.4">Sender refuses to send the X display location.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.5">IAC DO X-DISPLAY-LOCATION</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.6">Sender is willing to receive the X display location in a
+subsequent sub-negotiation.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.7">IAC DON'T X-DISPLAY-LOCATION</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.8">Sender refuses to accept the X display location.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.9">IAC SB X-DISPLAY-LOCATION SEND IAC SE</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.10">Sender requests receiver to transmit his (the receiver's) X
+display location.  The code for SEND is 1.  (See below.)</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.11">IAC SB X-DISPLAY-LOCATION IS ... IAC SE</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.12">Sender is stating his X display location.  The code for IS is
